{
  "slug": "membase",
  "name": "Membase",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Membase connects Claude Code to Membase Cloud, giving Claude persistent memory and wiki workflows across coding sessions. It can recall relevant prior context before prompts, save durable project decisions and user preferences, and search stable wiki documents while you work.\n\nThe plugin includes slash commands, MCP tools, project-aware recall, optional summary capture, and privacy safeguards for avoiding secrets, raw source files, and private blocks.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **5 skills**, **1 agent**, **8 commands**, **4 hooks** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (5): `memory-hygiene` (Correct, avoid, or delete unsafe or stale Membase context), `project-context` (Capture durable repository-specific context into Membase), `recall` (Use Membase memory and wiki when prior user/project context may improve the answer), `remember` (Store durable user or project context in Membase safely), `wiki` (Store and retrieve factual documents, references, and stable project knowledge in Membase wiki)\n- **Agents** (1): `membase-curator` (Curate Claude Code session context into safe Membase memory or wiki summaries)\n- **Commands** (8): `index-project` (Prepare a project knowledge summary for Membase), `login` (Connect Claude Code to Membase with OAuth and choose auto-capture settings), `logout` (Disconnect Claude Code from Membase), `project-config` (View or set Membase project scoping for the current repo), `recall` (Search Membase memory and wiki explicitly), `remember` (Store explicit durable context in Membase), `status` (Check Membase auth, capture, project, spool, and duplicate MCP status), `wiki` (Search, add, update, or delete Membase wiki documents)\n- **Hooks** (4): `SessionStart`, `UserPromptSubmit`, `Stop`, `SessionEnd`\n- **MCP servers** (1): `membase`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install membase@claude-community` from `aristoapp/claude-membase` (`plugin`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
